---
import ReynoldsLayout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const lastUpdated = '10 August 2026';
---

<ReynoldsLayout
  title="Our Cookie Policy | Reynolds Dryline Consent Guide"
  description="Learn how Reynolds Dryline uses essential and analytics cookies on our UK website, and how to accept, reject or manage your consent choices."
  canonical="https://www.reynoldsdryline.co.uk/cookies"
>
  <PageHero
    title="Cookie Policy"
    subtitle="How cookies and similar technologies are used on this website."
    breadcrumb="Legal"
  />

  <section class="rd-section rd-section--surface px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 !mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. We also use similar
        technologies such as local storage. Together they help the Site work and, where you allow it,
        help us understand how it is used.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How we use cookies</h2>
      <p>We group cookies into two categories:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Essential</strong> — needed for security, forms, remembering your cookie choice, and
          basic Site operation. These always run.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics</strong> — optional. Used to measure visits and improve the Site. These only
          load if you accept analytics cookies.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Cookies and technologies we use</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="rd-cookie-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Name / tech</th>
              <th scope="col">Category</th>
              <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
              <th scope="col">Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>rd_cookie_consent</code></td>
              <td>Essential</td>
              <td>Stores your cookie preference (essential only or analytics allowed)</td>
              <td>180 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>rd_cookie_consent_v1</code> (local storage)</td>
              <td>Essential</td>
              <td>Remembers detailed consent choices in your browser</td>
              <td>Until cleared</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Netlify form / hosting cookies</td>
              <td>Essential</td>
              <td>Supports secure hosting and form submissions</td>
              <td>Session / provider-defined</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Netlify Identity (admin only)</td>
              <td>Essential</td>
              <td>Used for authorised CMS login to <code>/admin</code></td>
              <td>Session / provider-defined</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Dotwall monitor tracker</td>
              <td>Analytics</td>
              <td>Website analytics and usage monitoring</td>
              <td>Only if accepted; provider-defined</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The Site may also load third-party resources that are not analytics cookies, such as Google Fonts
        and map tiles (Leaflet / OpenStreetMap / CARTO) on pages that show a map. Those requests can involve
        technical data like IP address being processed by the provider.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Consent banner</h2>
      <p>
        On your first visit you will see a cookie banner. You can:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Accept all</strong> — allow essential and analytics cookies</li>
        <li><strong>Reject non-essential</strong> — essential only; analytics stays blocked</li>
        <li><strong>Manage</strong> — choose analytics on or off, then save</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Until you accept analytics, the Dotwall tracking script will not load.
      </p>
      <p>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="rd-cookie-policy-settings"
          class="rd-btn-outline-red !normal-case !tracking-normal !text-sm !font-semibold"
        >
          Change cookie settings
        </button>
      </p>

      <h2>5. Browser controls</h2>
      <p>
        You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings. If you block essential cookies,
        parts of the Site (for example forms or remembering preferences) may not work properly.
      </p>

      <h2>6. More information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a></li>
        <li><a href="/contact">Contact us</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@reynoldsltd.co.uk">info@reynoldsltd.co.uk</a><br />
        Telephone: <a href="tel:01509816600">01509 816 600</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline data-astro-rerun>
    (function () {
      var btn = document.getElementById('rd-cookie-policy-settings');
      if (!btn) return;
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (typeof window.rdOpenCookieSettings === 'function') {
          window.rdOpenCookieSettings();
        } else {
          document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('rd:open-cookie-settings'));
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</ReynoldsLayout>

<style>
  .rd-cookie-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .rd-cookie-table th,
  .rd-cookie-table td {
    border: 1px solid rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.12);
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .rd-cookie-table th {
    background: #f6f7f8;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111827;
  }

  .rd-cookie-table code {
    font-size: 0.8em;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
</style>
